Function Name: performance_report
Description: Generates an employee performance report using data from performance_reviews.csv. Supports three report types: summary (returns employee_id, overall_rating as float, and goals_status for a specific employee), detailed (returns all original CSV fields and types for a specific employee), and department (returns a department-wise aggregation with average overall_rating as float and employee count).
Parameters:
- employee_id (optional string): The employee_id to look up. If None, triggers department-reporting mode.
- report_type (string, default "summary"): Selects the report mode. Options are "summary", "detailed", or "department".
Example:
1. performance_report(employee_id="E123", report_type="summary")
   → { "employee_id": "E123", "overall_rating": 4.5, "goals_status": "Achieved" }
2. performance_report(employee_id="E123", report_type="detailed")
   → { "employee_id": "E123", "employee_name": "...", ..., "overall_rating": 4.5, ... }
3. performance_report(employee_id=None, report_type="department")
   → { "Sales": { "avg_rating": 4.16, "count": 12 }, "IT": { "avg_rating": 3.98, "count": 10 }, ... }
Composition: Would read "/home/aifahim/PycharmProjects/Self-Adapting-AI-Agent/dataset/performance_tracker/performance_reviews.csv", filter/group as required.
Return Types and Field Specifications:
- summary mode: { "employee_id": (string), "overall_rating": (float), "goals_status": (string) }
- detailed mode: { all columns preserved, original types }
- department mode: { department_name: { "avg_rating": (float), "count": (int) }, ... }
